## Working with Claude Code

This project uses a Claude Code harness scaffolded from [claude-scaffold](https://github.com/ajinkya-t/claude-scaffold).

Key conventions:
- One chat per task; for parallel work, create a `git worktree` and start a fresh Claude session there
- `/plan` before non-trivial work, `/review` before `/commit`, `/techdebt` at end of session
- Agent instructions live in `AGENTS.md` (vendor-neutral, read by Codex/Cursor/Aider too)
- Settings, hooks, subagents, and skills in `.claude/`
{%- if chrome_extension %}
- Frontend work: install the Claude in Chrome extension for live-page verification
{%- endif %}
{%- if enable_bmad %}
- For substantial features: consider BMAD Method for spec-first elicitation (https://github.com/bmad-code-org/BMAD-METHOD)
{%- endif %}

